From 74177e92f029550b4b7faf8db4e0b90c2226f082 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cole Walker <cole.walker@windriver.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 10:56:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ptp4l, ts2phc, phc2sys: gearshift mechanism
 (Park/Neutral/Drive)

Enables dynamic switching between Park, Neutral, and Drive modes via
PMC management messages (MID_GEARSHIFT_NP 0xC0F0, MID_GEAR_STATUS_NP
0xC0F1). This allows safe coexistence of multiple timing applications
sharing a PHC when switching between GNSS and PTP sources.
  - Park: No PHC updates, no servo processing
  - Neutral: Servo runs but PHC adjustments suppressed
  - Drive: Normal operation (default)
  - Servo reset on PARK->DRIVE transition
  - Config file option: gear=P|N|D
Based on Intel LinuxPTP 4.4 gearshift delivery, ported to 4.2.

Signed-off-by: Cole Walker <cole.walker@windriver.com>
