+.SH GEARSHIFT
+The gearshift mechanism controls whether this ptp4l instance is permitted
+to discipline the PHC.
+
+.TP
+.B D (Drive)
+The servo is active and PHC adjustments are applied. This is the default
+behavior if no gear is specified.
+
+.TP
+.B N (Neutral)
+The servo continues running, but PHC adjustments are suppressed.
+
+.TP
+.B P (Park)
+Monitor-only mode. No servo operation and no PHC adjustments are applied.
+
+The active gear may be queried or changed at runtime using PMC management
+commands (see pmc(8)).
+
 .SH SEE ALSO
 .BR pmc (8),
 .BR phc2sys (8)
