+.TP
+.B ts2phc.seed_system_time
+When set to 1, if the PPS source is \fBnmea\fP and no valid RMC sentence has been received yet, \fBts2phc\fP will seed the Time-of-Day from the system clock (\fBCLOCK_REALTIME\fP) and align it to the PPS boundary, effectively behaving as if an initial satellite fix were present. Once a valid NMEA timestamp is available, the program will use it. The default is 0 (disabled).
+
+.SH GEARSHIFT
+The gearshift mechanism determines whether this ts2phc instance is
+allowed to discipline the PHC.
+
+.TP
+.B D (Drive)
+GNSS-sourced PHC discipline is enabled. This is the default mode.
+
+.TP
+.B N (Neutral)
+GNSS data continues to be processed, but PHC adjustments are suppressed.
+
+.TP
+.B P (Park)
+Monitor-only mode. No PHC discipline occurs.
+
+Gear may be modified at runtime via PMC commands directed at the ts2phc
+management socket (see pmc(8)).
+
 .SH SEE ALSO
 .BR phc2sys (8)
 .BR ptp4l (8)
